From 565ce63b9cd92423385ae8f2033b62ef22167220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toly <1397674+AnatolyRugalev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:28:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: an inline SVG's <image> draws what the document
 fetches for it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An inline <svg>'s <image href> loaded a data: URL and nothing else (0006):
usvg resolves hrefs as it parses, and the fork's resolver refused all but
data:. So an <image> could not show a resource the page's NetProvider
serves, a cid: one in HOTTY (SPEC §7.1 names SVG href), or an image from
the network a policy allows (§7.2's img-src covers images in SVG).

An SVG <image> is now fetched like an <img>: when it joins the document
or its href (or xlink:href) changes, through the NetProvider, as
destination Image. Its bytes are kept by resolved URL
(BaseDocument::svg_images, svg_image.rs), and when they arrive the
outermost <svg> it is in is constructed, and so parsed, again. The
resolver usvg is given hands it those bytes, by href as written; it
still reads no file. reload_resource_by_href fetches such an image again,
so a resource sent again shows. data: URLs stay usvg's. An SVG that is
itself an image (an <img>, a CSS image) still loads nothing but data:,
as in a browser.

an_image_draws_what_the_document_fetched_for_it checks the resolver.
hotty-blitz's an_inline_svgs_image_resolves_cid_resources (sent before,
after, and again) and an_inline_svgs_images_are_images (the network)
check the whole path; the first fails without the change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
